course: dictionary
lesson: 13870
title: A boat with two masts
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A ketch is a word for a kind of boat. When you meet a new word, look at the words around it, because they often give you clues. «The little ketch bobbed gently in the harbour.» A boat that bobs gently in a harbour is floating on the water, so a ketch must be a boat.
explain: The sentence «The ketch had two masts, and the front one was taller.» tells you more. A mast is the tall pole that holds up a boat's sail. A ketch has two of them: a taller one at the front and a shorter one near the back. Picture it, then check with the words in the sentence.
explain: Sometimes a word has more than one meaning. In old dialect, «ketch» was another way of saying «catch». When you read about sailing or the sea, a ketch means the sailing boat, so use the clues in the story to decide.
fact: A ketch is a sailing boat with two masts.
fact: In a ketch, the taller mast is at the front and the shorter mast is near the back.
fact: A mast is the tall pole that holds up the sails on a boat.
fact: The word «ketch» is a noun, so it names a thing: a ketch, two ketches.
fact: Check a new word by swapping in your meaning: «Grandad steered the sailing boat with two masts across the bay» still makes sense.
exercise: «The little ketch bobbed gently in the harbour.» What is a ketch? | A large car used on farms | A type of fish | A small house by the sea | *A sailing boat with two masts
exercise: «The ketch had two masts, and the front one was taller.» How many masts did the ketch have? | Three | Four | *Two | One
exercise: Find and copy the word that names the boat in «Grandad steered the ketch across the bay.» | steered | bay | *ketch | Grandad
test: Which mast is shorter on a ketch? | The mast at the front | *The mast near the back | The harbour wall | The sail
test: Mia says a ketch is a kind of bird. What does ketch really mean? | A small fish | A bag for shopping | A bird that swims | *A sailing boat with two masts
exam: What does ketch mean in «Tom sailed the ketch out of the harbour, and its two masts caught the wind»? | A kind of hat | *A sailing boat with two masts | A shop near the quay | A tall tower by the sea
